  "internal_policy": {
    "CATA_720": "One Battlecry body captures both original physical decks in player1/player2 order and each deck order. Select current stored local_cost amount<=2 (not hand/player quote or printed-only cost), capture CardReferences once, then one DestroyDeckBatch. All selected movements precede destruction reactions; no requery, discard, minion death/corpse or fatigue.",
    "FIR_922": "Actual 1mana1Attack2durability weapon Battlecry. Requires original source still the captured player actual equipped weapon, live and positive durability. Own current HAND must contain MINION with native public_gifts identity; ordinary equal stats, deck/board/opponent minions do not qualify. ModifyWeapon(original id,attack3) only; no durability gain or generated pool.",
    "JAIL_030": "Native attack_finished and completed_attack fact: original self actual attacker, real combat, matching original source epoch/entry/card, live/healthy at accepted finish snapshot. Draw1 first then RemoveFromGame on same captured MinionReference. Draw reactions can retire/return/transform/control source so stale removal skips. No death/deathrattle/corpse; cancelled attacks, defending, other attackers and bare CombatDamage do not qualify. Terminal draw consequences stop tail through existing scheduler.",
    "MEND_805": "Un-schooled SPELL. death_candidates(DeathQuery(side=friendly,min_turn=current global turn,max_turn=same)) captures ordered separate BOARD MINION deaths by controller-at-death once. Each original DeathRecord goes to existing CopyCard(mode=base,HAND), preserving current death face, physical components and supported innate identity. Existing SummonStats(original base_attack+3,base_health+3) creates base-recovery reward before acquisition notification; old local buffs, injury, silence and hand cost do not transfer. Repeated deaths of same physical entity remain separate copies, no entity/card dedup. This printed-base stat recipe and exact copy/acquisition windows remain CN-uncalibrated. Baseline has no registered Jade or Cthun profiles; no such unsupported family is invented for this adapter.",
    "evidence": "Four complete fixed37.0 raw records and eight full official en-US/zh-CN faces, all without named child dependencies. Internal source/lifecycle/acceptance tests do not certify complete M0 formal pool or precise M6 server timing."
  },
  "formal_pool_complete": false,
  "cn_calibrated": false
}
